# Composer's "path" repository type (used by VERIFICATION.md's install instructions, and by any
# real consumer developing against this module via a local path repo) exports this repo's
# contents via git-archive-style rules when copying (options.symlink=false), so anything listed
# here as export-ignore is excluded from that copy - same as .gitignore is for git itself, but
# also enforced for people who DO have these paths present locally (e.g. dev tooling already
# installed) instead of just for a clean checkout.
#
# Found the hard way: without this, `vendor/` (this repo's own dev-tooling install - phpunit,
# phpstan, codeception, etc., needed for CI but not part of the shipped module) got copied
# straight into vendor/ordo/module-automation/vendor/ inside a consuming Magento install,
# duplicate-declaring classes (e.g. Codeception's own SuiteInitSubscriberTrait) and crashing
# `bin/magento setup:di:compile` with a fatal "Cannot redeclare trait" error.
/*.log export-ignore
/.idea/ export-ignore
/.magento_cache/ export-ignore
/.php-cs-fixer.cache export-ignore
/.phpunit.result.cache export-ignore
/.playwright-mcp/ export-ignore
/clover.xml export-ignore
/junit.xml export-ignore
/node_modules/ export-ignore
/vendor/ export-ignore
